<article class="env-lemma" id="09V9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09V9">Lemma <span data-tag="09V9">20.47.10</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ be a ringed space. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ viewed as an object of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ is $0$-pseudo-coherent if and only if $\mathcal{F}$ is a finite type $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ viewed as an object of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ is $(-1)$-pseudo-coherent if and only if $\mathcal{F}$ is an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module of finite presentation. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Use Lemma <a href="/tag/08DN" data-tag="08DN">20.47.9</a> to prove the implications in one direction and Lemma <a href="/tag/09V8" data-tag="09V8">20.47.8</a> for the other. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>